[Throughout the following it is assumed that the daggers have same 
id-status, buc-status and enchantment so that they are eligible to merge.]

An unnamed dagger that is picked up or taken out of a container merges 
with first (in terms of inventory letters) stack of daggers.

So if you have: a - a +0 dagger named A and b - a +0 dagger named B and 
you pick up a +0 dagger it'll end up to the inventory letter a.

Even if you have: a - a +0 dagger and b - a +0 dagger named BONES and 
you pick up a +0 dagger it'll end up to the inventory letter a.

If you have installed the counted adjustment patch then getting two 
stacks of daggers is trivial: just adjust some of them onto a different 
inventory letter.

If you haven't installed the patch then this is how it can be done:

1. Name the daggers with the first name.
2. Then drop those you want to retain the name.
3. Rename the rest with a second name.
4. Pick up the daggers that were dropped.

